@prefix gmeow:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix owl:    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix semapv: <https://w3id.org/semapv/vocab/> .
@prefix bfo:    <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/> .

# Term equivalences for the mentation slice — GMEOW authoring source.
# Compiled to mappings/gmeow-mentation.sssom.tsv by `gmeow compile-mappings`.
# All alignments are BY REFERENCE (Principle 5); GMEOW never imports an external axiom.

gmeow:mapsetMentation a gmeow:MappingSet ;
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-mentation.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:setId "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/mappings/mentation" ;
    gmeow:license "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
    gmeow:setComment """Mentation slice alignments — the occurrent (perdurant) half of mind.

        AXIOMATIC PARENT (not a mapping row): gmeow:MentalProcess rdfs:subClassOf gmeow:Event, and
        gmeow:Event is grounded in gUFO's gufo:Event — the gUFO Event axiom is imported transitively
        via the events slice, not as a mapping row.

        EXTERNAL BRIDGES NAMED IN PROSE (no stable, resolvable RDF namespace available):
        * Cognitive Atlas (cognitiveatlas.org): 'cognitive process' and 'mental process' concepts
          (e.g. reasoning, perception, attention, imagery) closely match the gmeow:MentalProcessType
          value vocabulary; the Cognitive Atlas uses ad-hoc numeric IRIs inside an undeclared namespace
          and no OWL-resolvable ontology file, so no TermEquivalence row can be written — the
          conceptual alignment is documented here instead.
        * Cognitive Paradigm Ontology (cpo, cogpo.org): maps cognitive tasks and paradigms to mental
          constructs; broadly aligns with the gmeow:MentalProcessType seed vocabulary but exposes no
          stable OWL-resolvable namespace for term-level alignment.
        * Mental Functioning Ontology (MFOEM, purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mfoem.owl): provides a BFO-based
          taxonomy of mental processes; BFO_0000015 ('process') is the closest alignable IRI
          (see the mapping row below); MFOEM's finer-grained mental process subclasses (e.g.
          MFOEM:MentalProcess) are not resolvable as stable IRIs in the OBO Foundry published OWL
          and are therefore named in prose only.
        * SUMO (ontologyportal.org): IntentionalProcess and Reasoning are conceptually adjacent to
          gmeow:MentalProcess and gmeow:processReasoning; the SUMO OWL serialization IRIs
          (ontologyportal.org/SUMO.owl#...) are not resolvable over HTTPS, so SUMO alignments are
          named in prose here rather than as TermEquivalence rows.""" ;
    gmeow:setTrailer "# No frame-selecting mapping (Principle 9): GMEOW does not assert a single 'correct' mental process taxonomy; value-vocab members are co-equal." .

# BFO 'process' (BFO_0000015) — a mental process IS a process in the BFO sense.
# Confidence is moderate: BFO process is broad (any occurrent with temporal extension
# that is not a temporal region), and gmeow:MentalProcess adds the experiencer/mind
# constraint; the overlap is genuine but the semantics are not identical.
gmeow:MentalProcess skos:relatedMatch bfo:BFO_0000015 {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-mentation.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.5 ;
    gmeow:comment "a mental process is a process (BFO_0000015: a occurrent that has some temporal proper part and is not a temporal region); loose match — BFO process is very broad and does not imply an experiencer"
|} .
